1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Procurement teams often review one tender feed
for several supplier profiles.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
TenderVerdict turns each notice into a human
next step: open, watch, or skip.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The workflow starts with synthetic supplier profiles
and normalized notice metadata.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Files stay on this Mac. Before analysis, a preview shows counts,
sample records, and metadata gaps.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
One canonical engine evaluates the same notices
and review date for every profile.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
It returns three verdicts: Open documents, Watch, or Reject,
with visible reasons. A human decides what to do next.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Free is a complete first-profile workflow,
not a disabled demo.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:52,000
It includes the full queue, verdict reasoning, supplied source links,
a shareable review brief, and deterministic schema-three JSON export.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Portfolio Workspace applies the same feed
to up to five independent supplier profiles.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:08,000
RevenueCat unlocks comparison and full portfolio export,
but never changes a verdict, creates a score, or makes a bid recommendation.

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
In the verified Test Store baseline, the Apple SDK
loaded a development-only purchase sheet.

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,500
CustomerInfo then confirmed
the entitlement was active.

13
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:23,000
It was not an App Store payment.
No real charge occurred.

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:31,000
For this evaluation build, RevenueCat Judge Access
grants the entitlement without a purchase.

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:39,000
A fresh check unlocked the screen. Restoring access, returning to the foreground,
and a full relaunch all kept the workspace unlocked.

16
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Synthetic data. No usable key is stored.
This is not production billing.

17
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
TenderVerdict is open-source macOS software
under Apache two point zero.
